cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite it as below."
title: "msr-qspr: grouped QSPR modeling of molar solubilization ratios for surfactant screening"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-11-23"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24464886"
abstract: >-
  msr-qspr predicts the molar solubilization ratio (MSR) of hydrophobic organic
  contaminants in aqueous surfactant solutions for preliminary surfactant
  screening in surfactant-enhanced aquifer remediation. It compares QSPR
  procedures under grouped, leakage-safe validation and provides model
  selection, applicability assessment, interpretation, target randomization,
  holdout evaluation, surfactant screening and a local prediction application.
repository-code: "https://github.com/jjara01/msr-qspr-sear"
